frontends/nss: restart the stats sync when a reply goes missing

The connection stats sync is a chain of CONN_STATS_SYNC_MANY requests in
which only the reply's callback queues the next request. If a reply is
lost, nothing re-queues the work and the sync stops until ECM is
reloaded. Conntrack then no longer gets counters or timeout refreshes for
accelerated connections and expires them while the firmware is still
forwarding, so later packets from the far side are rejected for having
no state.

Tag each request with a sequence number in app_data and arm a 5 seconds
timeout after sending it. If no matching reply arrives in time, count it in
stats_request_counter, warn, and restart the walk from index 0. A late
reply to an abandoned request still has its records applied but does not
advance the chain.

Signed-off-by: Manuel Fombuena <fombuena@outlook.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
